# Personal Planner Provisioning Control-Plane Hardening Record

## Review history

The Terra production review and focused Sol review confirmed two Critical issues: an ambiguous project-create result could reach a second create request without mandatory reconciliation, and a delayed OAuth callback could write Management credentials after expiry cleanup. They also confirmed three Important issues: verification transport uncertainty was incorrectly terminal, migration/verification calls lacked durable in-flight ownership, and migration recovery was not reachable from its generic recoverable state.

## Implemented resolutions

- Project creation now uses `project_reconciliation_required` and `project_retry_authorized`, a durable create nonce, and a 90-second create lease. Only initial organization selection or a durable, authoritative zero-match reconciliation result can reserve a POST. One match recovers the recorded ref; multiple matches become terminal; inconclusive reconciliation remains recoverable without a new POST. Completion and uncertainty handling require the active nonce.
- OAuth state is stored with a SHA-256 state hash. Callback credential persistence performs encryption first, then synchronously reloads and validates current authorization state, one-time callback claim, state hash, token lifetime, and transaction TTL immediately before its durable write. It clears OAuth state/hash/verifier on success. Expiry clears those values and encrypted Management material.
- Capability authentication performs its final state/expiry check after asynchronous hashing. Management-token decryption also rechecks current transaction authority and ciphertext identity after decrypting.
- Verification is explicitly `passed`, `assertion_failed`, or `indeterminate`. Only fixed-verification assertion failure becomes terminal. 429/5xx/network/malformed responses retain bounded retryable verification state and authority until ready or TTL expiry.
- Migration and verification have durable operation kind/nonces and leases. Active duplicate calls return in-progress. Completion validates its nonce. A stale migration lease first moves to `migration_reconciliation_required`; the next migration call reads official history before any POST. Canonical drift remains terminal and fail-closed.
- Project readiness is checked through the Management project-status endpoint before migrations. A not-yet-healthy project becomes retryable migration reconciliation, not migration-history drift or another project-create attempt.

## Regression coverage

`provisioning_poc/test/production.test.ts` now covers create reservation/reconciliation constraints, active leases, bounded retry authorization, OAuth expiry/replay predicates, actual expired-callback rejection, nonce-bound migration/verification completion, migration recovery transitions and canonical history behavior, verification assertion-versus-transport classification, and secret redaction. The suite has 14 passing focused tests.

## Validation

- `npm run check` — passing.
- `npm test` — passing: 14 tests.
- `npm run deploy:dry` — passing; Worker bundle reports only the existing Durable Object binding.
- `git diff --check` — passing.

## Scope and remaining items

No Flutter source, Planner migrations, `planner_testing`, or hosted Supabase projects were touched. The only Cloudflare persistence mechanism is the existing SQLite-backed Durable Object; no D1, KV, R2, Queues, Workflows, Hyperdrive, or additional Worker was introduced.

The external release dependency remains: Supabase Management migration API entitlement for arbitrary unrelated end-user organizations is not externally confirmed. This does not change the tested control-plane mechanics, but must be confirmed before public release. No fallback transport has been introduced.

